<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 2132) <span class="when">Nov 3, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Improvements and fixes.</b></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 2128) <span class="when">Nov 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Quitting no longer crashes</b> while EXR frames are still being read.</li>
<li><b>Improvements and fixes.</b></li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2107) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Improvements and fixes.</b></li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2104) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Improvements and fixes.</b></li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2102) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Comment subtitles follow the host</b> when they turn them on for everyone, at their position unless you chose your own.</li>
<li><b>Fixed:</b> joining a review of cut movies could show "Proxy stream failed… Cannot Open". Asobi Review now waits for the host's copy of the movie and tries again.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2098) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Notes read the movie's timecode,</b> as the burn-in does.</li>
<li><b>Start Timecode…</b> in Playback ▸ Source sets where a movie's timecode starts.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2093) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Every comment of a cut movie in one list:</b> the Notes tab's Whole movie lists every shot's comments; click a timecode to go there.</li>
<li>Comment subtitles are in the bar's Show menu too.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2089) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Every shot of a long cut movie fits in the strip:</b> the last few shots no longer sit past the window's edge.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
